# Phase 4 - Monitoring and Logging

## Goal
Enable visibility into AWS account activity and resource behavior.

## Services Used
- AWS CloudTrail (audit logging)
- Amazon CloudWatch (metrics and monitoring)

## CloudTrail Setup

Created a CloudTrail trail named HybridCloudLab-Trail in us-east-2.

Configured logging for both read and write management events to capture AWS API activity such as EC2 launches, security group changes, and networking modifications.

Logs are stored in an S3 bucket for persistent audit records.

## CloudTrail Event Review

Observed CloudTrail events corresponding to EC2 and networking actions within the lab environment.

Verified that CloudTrail logs AWS API activity such as instance state changes and security group modifications.

## CloudWatch Review

Reviewed EC2 metrics using CloudWatch, including CPU utilization and network traffic.

Observed baseline system behavior and confirmed that monitoring is functioning.

CloudWatch provides operational visibility into system performance and resource health.

## Monitoring Insight

CloudTrail and CloudWatch provide different types of visibility:

- CloudTrail logs AWS API actions (who did what and when)
- CloudWatch monitors system performance and behavior

Together, they provide both audit and operational visibility.
